{"availability":"available","full":"fazal305/bijli-bill-explainer","name":"bijli-bill-explainer","description":"Urdu-first web app that reads a photo of a Pakistani electricity bill and explains, line by line in plain Urdu, where the money went and why the bill went up.","category":"Finance","language":"JavaScript","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2026-10-05T08:02:48Z","updated":"2026-10-05T08:11:48Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://bijli-bill-explainer.vercel.app","topics":["accessibility","electricity-bill","pakistan","react","urdu","vercel","vite"],"demo":"https://bijli-bill-explainer.vercel.app/","color":"#63362a","ink":"#f8c7a8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-06T15:46:13.573Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-06T15:46:13.573Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-06T15:46:13.573Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-06T15:46:13.573Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":["React"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Pakistani electricity bills are full of lines that even grown children struggle to explain to their parents: FPA, QTR, F.C. Surcharge, Electricity Duty, GST, and a units total that quietly crossed a slab. This Urdu-first web app takes a photo of the bill (K-Electric, LESCO, FESCO, IESCO, PEPCO and the other distribution companies) and explains, line by line in plain Urdu, where the money went and why the bill went up.","Screenshots show the app's built-in sample bill, which is made up and labelled as a sample.","The model's only job is transcription: amounts, units, the bill month and the monthly history table, each line mapped to one of 18 known keys (fpa, qta, fcsurcharge, gst…). The Urdu meaning of each line comes from a fixed dictionary (src/lib/dictionary.js). \"Why did it go up?\" is worked out by plain rules in src/lib/explain.js:"],"features":["units compared with last month, from the bill's own history table;","crossing 200 units after six months below it (losing \"protected\" status);","crossing a 100-unit slab boundary;","a fuel price a